BT 1 0 0 1 0 189.888 Tm .66525 Tw 18 TL /F4 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (2019 Bar Q: In January 2016, Mr. H was issued a life insurance policy by XYZ Insurance) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.129538 Tw (Co., wherein his wife, Mrs. W, was designated as the sole beneficiary. Unbeknownst to) Tj T* 0 Tw .410769 Tw (XYZ Insurance Co., however, Mr. H had been previously diagnosed with colon cancer, the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.2448 Tw (fact of which Mr. H had concealed during the entire time his insurance policy was being) Tj T* 0 Tw .444 Tw (processed. In January 2019, Mr. H unfortunately committed suicide. Due to her husband's) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.265714 Tw (death, Mrs. W, as beneficiary, filed a claim with XYZ Insurance Co. to recover the) Tj T* 0 Tw .051429 Tw (proceeds of the late Mr. H's life insurance policy. However, XYZ Insurance Co. resisted the) Tj T* 0 Tw .403714 Tw (claim, contending that: 1. the policy is void ab initio because Mr. H fraudulently concealed) Tj T* 0 Tw .354 Tw (or misrepresented his medical condition, i.e., his colon cancer; and 2. as an insurer in a life) Tj T* 0 Tw .3735 Tw (insurance policy, it cannot be held liable in case of suicide. Rule on each of XYZ Insurance) Tj T* 0 Tw (Co.'s contentions. \(5%\)) Tj T* ET
