BT 1 0 0 1 0 171.804 Tm .055059 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: Both of XYZ's contentions fail because by January 2019 the policy had been in force for three) Tj T* 0 Tw .1392 Tw (years, so the Sec. 48 two-year incontestability bar kills the concealment defense and the Sec. 183) Tj T* 0 Tw (two-year suicide clock makes the suicide compensable.) Tj  T* .38175 Tw (The controlling rules are Sec. 48, under which the insurer is barred after two years from proving) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.053714 Tw (void ab initio or rescission for fraud or concealment even on a void-ab-initio recast \(Manila) Tj T* 0 Tw .0944 Tw (Bankers\), and Sec. 183, which makes the insurer liable for suicide committed after the policy has) Tj T* 0 Tw (been in force two years from issue or last reinstatement.) Tj  T* 1.632 Tw (Applied here, three years in force exceeds both clocks, so the concealed colon cancer can no) Tj T* 0 Tw (longer be proved to avoid the policy and the sane suicide after the period is a covered risk.) Tj  T* (XYZ must therefore pay Mrs. W the proceeds of the policy.) Tj T* ET
