BT 1 0 0 1 0 243.804 Tm 4.776923 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The claim is recoverable under both the authorized-driver and theft covers, so the) Tj T* 0 Tw (Commission's dismissal of the own-damage and theft claim must be set aside.) Tj  T* 3.713 Tw (The controlling rules are Sec. 439, which lets the Commissioner adjudicate the insured's) Tj T* 0 Tw .6256 Tw (own-damage and theft claim up to P5,000,000.00 with appeal by notice to the Court of Appeals) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.4368 Tw (within thirty \(30\) days. The adhesion-construction rule resolves policy ambiguities strictly) Tj T* 0 Tw .248 Tw (against the insurer. Art. 308 of the Revised Penal Code treats unlawful taking without consent as) Tj T* 0 Tw (theft because use itself is gain.) Tj  T* 4.551273 Tw (Applied here, entrusting the key to an established repair shop presumptively authorizes) Tj T* 0 Tw .69075 Tw (legitimate driving by a licensed driver, so the diversion to an illicit purpose does not breach the) Tj T* 0 Tw .816 Tw (clause. The taking without consent is theft regardless of permanence, and here it proved lasting) Tj T* 0 Tw (since the car was smashed beyond serviceable return.) Tj  T* 1.243 Tw (Villacorta therefore recovers P35,000.00 with legal interest from filing, subject to the insurer's) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.671 Tw (subrogation against the shop, and the remedy from the adverse ruling is a Sec. 439 notice of) Tj T* 0 Tw (appeal to the Court of Appeals filed with the Commissioner within thirty \(30\) days from receipt.) Tj T* ET
