BT 1 0 0 1 0 207.804 Tm 1.418769 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: Both transactions are barred as proposed because each crosses a control-line threshold that) Tj T* 0 Tw (needs prior clearance.) Tj  T* .102857 Tw (The controlling rules are Sec. 290\(b\), which presumes control where a person holds forty percent) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.006571 Tw (\(40%\) or more of voting securities. Sec. 299 requires prior written approval for a controlled) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.269 Tw (insurer's transactions with its holding-company system involving five percent \(5%\) or more of) Tj T* 0 Tw .647077 Tw (admitted assets. Sec. 302\(a\) requires twenty \(20\) days written notice plus prior written approval) Tj T* 0 Tw (for a non-insurer's acquisition of control of a domestic insurer.) Tj  T* 3.136615 Tw (Applied here, the six-percent asset sale exceeds the five-percent line and falls outside the) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.3768 Tw (thirty-day notice band for smaller transactions, while the forty-five-percent stock purchase) Tj T* 0 Tw (exceeds the forty-percent presumption and is an acquisition of control by a non-insurer.) Tj  T* .343636 Tw (Neither transaction may therefore proceed without the required approvals: prior written approval) Tj T* 0 Tw (for the sale, and twenty-day notice plus prior written approval for the acquisition.) Tj T* ET
