BT 1 0 0 1 0 153.804 Tm .600857 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The cancellation is invalid, and the company must accept reinstatement or reimburse the late) Tj T* 0 Tw (payments.) Tj  T* 1.841143 Tw (The controlling rule is Sec. 23, which requires a 60-day grace period, a 2-year reinstatement) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.516 Tw (window from grace lapse with no cancellation inside it, and two written 30-day notices - one) Tj T* 0 Tw (after grace expiry and one after reinstatement-period expiry.) Tj  T* .383143 Tw (Applied here, six months of nonpayment still falls inside the reinstatement window, and a single) Tj T* 0 Tw (notice fails the two-notice rule.) Tj  T* .979385 Tw (Cancellation is therefore barred until the window closes with both notices given. The company) Tj T* 0 Tw (must accept reinstatement or reimburse.) Tj T* ET
